-- 2410_fix_easy_medium_intensity_label_swap.sql
--
-- UI_E2E 2026-08-05 row 32 (HIGH): 'Gentle Start' Wk1 Easy tier prescribes
-- MORE reps than Medium for every exercise -- the intensity ladder is inverted.
--
-- ROOT CAUSE (confirmed by a full-catalog scan of all 46 Zealova Library
-- programs' Easy/Medium variant pairs, comparing every exercise's `reps` value
-- week-by-week, day-by-day): the program_variants.intensity_level LABEL was
-- swapped onto the wrong row at generation time for 15 programs, where 100% of
-- exercise-reps comparisons show Easy > Medium (the row LABELED Easy holds the
-- content that is actually gentler than what's labeled Medium, and vice versa).
-- The program_variant_weeks schedule CONTENT itself is untouched and correctly
-- authored -- only the label pointing to it was wrong, so this fix swaps
-- intensity_level + the Easy/Medium substring of variant_name between the two
-- rows of each pair. No workout content (sets/reps/exercises) is modified.
--
-- SCOPE: only the 15 programs where the inversion is EXACTLY 100% (a clean
-- full swap) are fixed here. 11 sibling programs show PARTIAL inversion rates
-- (49-96%) -- swapping labels there would not cleanly fix them (some exercises
-- already agree with their label) and risks making things worse; those need a
-- generator-level review / possible regeneration, flagged separately, NOT
-- included in this migration.
--
-- MECHANICS: program_variants has a UNIQUE(base_program_id, intensity_level,
-- duration_weeks, sessions_per_week) constraint that is NOT deferrable, so a
-- direct Easy<->Medium swap collides mid-transaction (both rows would
-- momentarily read the same key). Each pair therefore does a 4-step swap: bump
-- the Easy row's sessions_per_week by +1000 (a harmless, unconstrained escape
-- value -- sessions_per_week has no CHECK constraint) to clear the collision,
-- flip both intensity_level + variant_name, then restore sessions_per_week.

-- Dumbbell Home Strength (Zealova Library) (15 Easy/Medium pairs)
